[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Its own cause table already shows a
second cause, and its footnote hides a third. Each one needs its own fix, so each now has its own
ticket.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} repo="https://github.com/zalio-pl/mega-support-kb" issues={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, shift: 3 }} />

<Callout kind="warn">
The queued parser fix closes only the <code>parser</code> row. Reports from the other two rows
keep coming until their own fixes ship.
</Callout>

## The three problems

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant writes the day
  first. Day and month swap: 7 April arrives as 4 July.
- **`hint`**: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at day-first tenants
  type month first, as told, and the form reads it day first. It looks like the parser bug, but
  the fix belongs in the form.
- **`shift`**: no swap. The date moves one day earlier (Tuesday shows as Monday, Lisbon gets
  Tuesday and Toronto gets Monday). Most likely a time zone or DST conversion. The desk had
  already read these reports as one-day moves.

## How the reports were placed

- Each report is counted once, by id. The ticket export repeats some rows.
- The tenant decides the cause, not the reporter's browser. Intake's tag is a guess and is
  ignored here (see `causes.ts`).
- The desk's one-day reading (`desk-notes.json`) beats placement by tenant.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject line alone. All three
problems produce the same subjects ("wrong day", "date is wrong"), so subject matching cannot keep
them apart. Splitting them needs the tenant, the channel and the body.

